`Deliver` receives non-nil callbacks. It must process events in input order, call `handle` only for the first occurrence of each event ID, and ignore later events with the same ID. After all unique events have been handled, it must call `complete` exactly once with the number of events delivered. An empty ID is a valid ID and is deduplicated normally.

```go
package solution

type Event struct {
	ID      string
	Payload string
}

func Deliver(events []Event, handle func(Event), complete func(int)) {
	for _, event := range events {
		handle(event)
	}
	complete(len(events))
}
```","reference_code":"package solution

